WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.953
A grid of land and water hides joined-up islands.

00:05.953 --> 00:14.700
Re-exploring from every land cell repeats the same ground over and over.

00:15.000 --> 00:19.555
Scan row by row instead.

00:19.555 --> 00:31.700
The first unclaimed land, at row 0, col 0, must be a new island.

00:32.000 --> 00:42.005
A queue floods from it to every joined square, claiming island 1.

00:42.005 --> 00:47.700
The scan moves on and finds two more.

00:48.000 --> 00:52.520
Each cell is claimed once: O(m·n).

00:52.520 --> 00:57.041
Three drops of ink, three islands.

00:57.041 --> 00:59.700
That’s graph search.

